# Time-boxed exceptions for the Keycloak image scan only (ADR-018 security gate). Each entry is a library
# bundled by upstream Keycloak 26.7.4 with no Keycloak release that updates it yet. Entries expire so the
# deploy gate fails again and forces a re-check; the fix is a Keycloak patch release, not a longer expiry.
# Reviewed 2026-09-26. Owner: platform engineering. Re-check every Keycloak 26.7.x release.

# SQL Server JDBC driver: we use PostgreSQL only (KC_DB=postgres); the driver is never loaded.
CVE-2025-59250 exp:2026-10-26

# Netty SNI routing bypass: TLS ends at Caddy; Keycloak serves plain HTTP on a private network, no SNI.
CVE-2026-75595 exp:2026-10-26

# FreeMarker path issue: affects untrusted templates; only Keycloak's built-in themes are installed and
# the administration console is not reachable from the internet.
CVE-2026-84939 exp:2026-10-26

# Bouncy Castle 1.84 (fixed in 1.85): not fully assessed; accepted as an upstream risk only until the next
# Keycloak patch. Mitigated by the private admin console and realm brute-force protection.
CVE-2026-8763 exp:2026-10-26
CVE-2026-13506 exp:2026-10-26

# jackson-databind 2.21.5 (fixed in 2.21.6): CPU denial of service through unbounded numeric parsing. Bundled by
# Keycloak 26.7.4 (also inside keycloak-admin-cli); no Keycloak release carries 2.21.6 yet. Denial of service
# only, no data or account access. Reachable JSON endpoints: the account API (signed-in customers only) and the
# admin API (private, not on the internet). Accepted by the owner on 2026-09-30 until the next Keycloak patch.
CVE-2026-68497 exp:2026-10-30
